<html lang="en">
<head>
    <title>Chat Message</title>
    <style>
        h3 { ${REGULAR_LARGE_FONT_STYLE} }
        body { ${REGULAR_FONT_STYLE} }
        code { ${MONOSPACE_FONT_STYLE} }
        h3 code { font-size: inherit; }
        p { margin-top:0; }

    </style>
</head>
<body>
    This is an overview of all tools available to the Database Assistant.<br>
    It allows you to determine which tools the language model can access.

    <br><br>
    You can manage tool access by approving or denying entire tool categories, as well as individual tools.

    The status of a tool determines its visibility and accessibility to the LLM:
    <ul>
        <li>Tools with unspecified approval status will be prompted for approval before every invocation.</li>
        <li>Tools marked as "Allowed" will be invoked automatically without supervision.</li>
        <li>Tools marked as "Denied" will fail with an authorization error upon invocation.</li>
        <li>Tools marked as "Hidden" will not be visible to the LLM.</li>
    </ul>
</body>

</html>
